## The core

This project takes the shared rules in `core/` by `core-manifest.md`, whose slots and names fill the core's words. What
a session reads is set by its role and its task: `node core/scripts/reading.mjs <role> --issue <the task's issue>` prints
it (the roles: `core/roles/`; a session whose brief names no role is a builder). A builder reads these whole at the
start of every task (Claude Code, Kiro and Antigravity pull them in through their entry files; any other tool: open each
file named), and any other role the manifest, the floor, its own file and what that names:

@core-manifest.md
@core/floor/security.md
@core/roles/builder.md
@core/modules/how-to-work.md
@core/modules/inbox.md
@core/modules/work-flow.md
@core/modules/git.md

The other files of the core are read when a task calls for them, each module saying when in its opening line, which the
script matches, among them `core/floor/topics.md` (when: the floor's opening says).

